### 3. The Sync Engine (`useSync.js`)
This hook checks for connectivity and pushes pending records to your API.

```javascript
import { useEffect } from 'react';
import { db } from './db';

export const useSync = () => {
  const syncData = async () => {
    const pending = await db.surveys.where('synced').equals(0).toArray();

    for (const record of pending) {
      try {
        await fetch('/api/surveys', {
          method: 'POST',
          body: JSON.stringify(record),
        });
        await db.surveys.update(record.id, { synced: 1 });
      } catch (err) {
        console.log("Still offline, keeping in local DB");
      }
    }
  };

  useEffect(() => {
    window.addEventListener('online', syncData);
    return () => window.removeEventListener('online', syncData);
  }, []);
};
```

### 4. Saving Data (The UI Component)
When the user submits a survey, we save it locally first. If the app is online, we trigger a sync immediately.

```jsx
