For this implementation, we will use **D3.js** with a **Treemap layout**. This is the industry standard for heatmaps because it handles hierarchical data and provides built-in zoom/pan capabilities via the `d3.zoom` behavior.

### 1. The Dependencies
Add these to your HTML `<head>`:
```html
<script src="https://d3js.org/d3.v7.min.js"></script>
<style>
    .node { cursor: pointer; stroke: #fff; stroke-width: 1px; }
    .label { font-size: 10px; fill: white; pointer-events: none; }
