    ```

#### 4. Busy-Waiting (No Sleeps)
Never use `std::this_thread::sleep_for` or `std::condition_variable`. These trigger a context switch to the kernel. A high-frequency system must "spin" (busy-wait), consuming 100% of the CPU core to ensure it is ready the microsecond data arrives.

