#### 1. Hardware Offloading (The "Secret Sauce")
In the code above, filtering happens in software. For sub-microsecond latency, you should use **`rte_flow`**. This allows you to offload the filtering logic directly to the NIC's ASIC (e.g., Mellanox ConnectX-6/7). The CPU never even sees the packets you want to drop.

#### 2. Busy Polling
Notice the `while(1)` loop. This is **Busy Polling**. We do not use interrupts (which cause context switches). We keep the CPU core at 100% usage constantly checking the NIC ring buffer. This eliminates the latency of waking up a sleeping CPU core.

