DPDK uses `mbufs` (memory buffers). When you receive a packet, you are receiving a pointer to the physical memory location on the NIC. By forwarding the same pointer (or modifying it in place), you achieve **Zero-Copy networking**, which is critical for staying under the 5-microsecond latency threshold.

