#### 1. Deterministic Timing (`std::this_thread::sleep_until`)
Using `sleep_until` based on an absolute clock is superior to `sleep_for`. If your control loop takes 2ms to execute, `sleep_for` would drift over time. `sleep_until` keeps the loop phase-aligned, ensuring jitter is minimized.

#### 2. Sensor Fusion Strategy
