To create a real-time 3D viewer, **Three.js** is the industry standard for the web. It abstracts WebGL, making it accessible while remaining powerful enough for complex shaders.

This implementation uses **Three.js** to render a 3D scene with **dynamic lighting** and a **custom GLSL shader** for a "pulsing" effect.

### 1. Project Setup
You can run this by creating an `index.html` file. No build tools are required.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <style>body { margin: 0; overflow: hidden; } canvas { display: block; }</style>
</head>
<body>
