### 2. The Physics World (Plugin Core)
This handles the "stepping" of the physics simulation. In a commercial engine, you would hook the `Update()` method into the engine's main tick loop.

```cpp
#include <vector>

class PhysicsEngine {
public:
    float damping = 0.99f;
    glm::vec3 gravity = glm::vec3(0.0f, -9.81f, 0.0f);

    void Step(std::vector<PhysicsParticle>& particles, float deltaTime) {
        for (auto& p : particles) {
            if (p.isStatic) continue;

            // Verlet Integration
            glm::vec3 velocity = (p.position - p.oldPosition) * damping;
            p.oldPosition = p.position;

            p.position += velocity + (p.acceleration * deltaTime * deltaTime);
            p.acceleration = gravity; // Reset acceleration
        }
    }
};
```

