Standard `Tick()` functions run once per frame. If your frame rate drops, your physics will "tunnel" through walls.
*   You must implement **Sub-stepping**. 
*   In Unreal, you override `OnRegisterPhysicsTickFunctions` to register your logic with the engine's `FPhysicsTickFunction`, which runs at a fixed frequency (e.g., 60Hz) regardless of the render frame rate.

